.TH elfshaker-esi-create 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi\-create \- Create an empty remote index
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi create\fR [OPTIONS] <ESI_FILE>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an empty remote index at ESI_FILE. VERSION selects the ESI wire format: v1 records pack and pack\-index checksums, while v2 also records their byte sizes. URL is the public URL of the index and is the base for relative pack URLs.
.PP
The command refuses to replace an existing file unless \-\-force is present. When it replaces a file, it saves the previous contents as ESI_FILE.bak unless \-\-no\-backup is present.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-meta\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
ESI wire format: v1 records checksums; v2 also records byte sizes.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
v1
.IP \(bu 2
v2
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Public URL of this index; relative pack URLs are resolved against it.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing ESI file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
Do not write .bak copies of the previous index contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIESI_FILE\fR>
ESI file to create.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a v2 index whose published URL is index.v2.esi:
.PP
.nf
\fBelfshaker esi create \-\-meta v2 \-\-url https://example.test/index.v2.esi index.v2.esi\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
elfshaker\-esi(1), elfshaker\-esi\-add(1), elfshaker\-clone(1)
